{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/880699-peach-the-great-solar-exalted-tournament","id":880699,"title":"[PEACH] The Great Solar Exalted Tournament","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Exalted","Solar Exalted"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-05-02T20:20:43-07:00","id":880699,"title":"[PEACH] The Great Solar Exalted Tournament","content":"<b>Preface:</b> for fun, I got together with one of my players and built two solars for the sole purpose of fighting each other and slugging it out till one fell. It was super fun, though a little disappointing that one came out on top each and every time with seemingly little effort. This tournament is an extension of that exercise as an idea I had while under the influence of Alcohol* and may have made certain promises to certain players that is see it through to the end. <br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:8px\">*We here at T.G.S.E.T. advise to Drink Responsibly</span><br /> <br /> <b>Concept:</b> 26 solar warriors gather together in the 'Austere and Glorious Arena of the Fifth Hand' each championing a different ability to the extreme of hyper-focus and putting them against each other's an elimination-style ladder tournament until there stands only one winner at the end who will be crowned &quot;Most OP Build&quot; <br /> <br /> <b>Rules:</b> Each Solar contestant is allocated a single ability which becomes their Supernal (relevant castes required). They follow the core book character creation process with only two exceptions. <br /> - No Charms purchased can be from an ability other than the one assigned to you (which also excludes Evocations)<br /> - No merits may provide an asset your ability cannot take advantage of directly (eg; Familiar for Survival Solar and Command for War Solar)<br /> <br /> To levy a fair and impartial battle, any abilities which require extreme situational environments take precedence over those that do not (Sail will always have a watery arena to battle within). Otherwise environments are allocated randomly from a set list. <br /> <br /> <b>Method of Running:</b> All battles will be run live at my gaming table, with one (maybe two) battles each week with the results and Play-by-Play being posted here for the forum to evaluate and dissect to their hearts content. If someone is interested in giving this a swing, send me a PM or post in this thread and I'll contact you. Games are run at +10GMT Melbourne Time so scheduling can be an issue for our international friends - you will be dialed in via Skype/Steam/ whatever voice chat you have access to. <br /> <br /> If anyone wants to submit a build, feel free. <br /> <br /> <b>Disclaimer:</b> I am in under no illusion as to the utter unfairness of pairing certain abilities against each other, but the purpose of the exercise is to see what abilities bring what elements to battle and to have heaps of fun doing it. Besides, the great and powerful Gee Says, God of Random Numbers will personally oversee all match ups and ensure no priority is given to to any particular ability. <br /> <br /> <br /> Let the Games Begin. <br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:28px\">Brawl VS Melee</span><br /> <br /> Wait, what, seriously!? Oh man. Ohh Kay.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>(10chars)","edited":{"userid":2721,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2721-elkovash","user":"Elkovash","date":". 05-02-2016, 11:24 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2721-elkovash","name":"Elkovash","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2721_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"528"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-02T21:13:31-07:00","id":880722,"title":"","content":"Well, this ought to be interesting.<br /> <br /> Brawl, Melee, and Martial Arts are all definitely strong contenders, since they're chock-full of combat Charms that are useful for both attack and defense.<br /> <br /> Archery and Thrown will probably be weaker, since they lack defenses and range is less useful in a duel than in group fights. But both have the potential to pull out a silly win. The broken-ness of Solar Spike might let Archery pull out a random win or two against &quot;better&quot; abilities.<br /> <br /> Resistance, Stealth, Awareness, Dodge, Occult, and Athletics all have some potential, but I doubt they'll make it too far. Without proper attack Charms, they'll have a hard time hurting the main contenders. Unless you let Occult bring in a horde of demons. Resistance, Stealth, and Dodge will at the very least be able to make the fight last a while.<br /> <br /> All that being said, my money is on War, Ride, or Survival. Your Merit rules give them hefty advantages. Maybe Brawl is better for fighting than Ride is, but is it better for fighting than Ride plus a Tyrant Lizard?<br /> <br /> If I didn't mention an ability here, I don't think it has a prayer.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/797631-why-craft-sucks-how-i-fixed-it\" target=\"_blank\">EX3 Craft Rewrite</a><br /> <br /> Sanctaphrax is not a person<br /> -Chejop Kejak","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1154-sanctaphrax","name":"Sanctaphrax","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1154_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1460"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-02T21:22:39-07:00","id":880731,"title":"","content":"I have to say, the Martial Artist Supernal is going to depend on which styles they pick.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Disclaimer: In favor of fun and enjoyment, but may speak up to warn you that you're gonna step on a metaphorical land mine","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2142-kyman201","name":"Kyman201","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2142_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4086"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-05T02:17:25-07:00","id":882693,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Okay so, no one has put their hands up for Melee so I'll handle it, but one of my players is a Brawl fanatic so he'll be handling the opponent.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">First off; we're probably going to get quite cheesy with our builds given that they are not intended to be long-game sustainable builds, so expect min-maxing. </span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Secondly; I didn't mention that even with the merit rule, I'm not banning artifact arms and armour otherwise we'll probably see a bunch of OHKO which is less dramatic and fun. The trade off of course is the mote limitation which, as a starting character we already don't have much of for sustained combat. </span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">With that said, let's meet our first contestant. </span></span><br /> <br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"font-size:20px\">Cathak Katsuko (Melee Supernal, Dawn Caste, Solar Exalted)</span></b><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">All the way from the Blessed Isle, Cathak Katsuko was a prodigy from the House of Bells who never exalted and at the age of twenty joined the Vermilion Legion to prove her righteousness for the next life. Little did she realize she's prove her worth in all the wrong ways. Touched by the Unconquered Sun after leading her brotherhood to a pyrrhic victory against a Raksha incursion in the northern isles she stands before us today as the champion of Melee Combat. </span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b>Build: </b>We're going to be focusing on the basic Melee multi-attack strategy here. The strength of this is we don't really mind how we engage, *something* sets off a chain of attacks and so landing those hits is more important than the individual damage they deal. Because we are a flexible ability, we can afford to load so heavily on offensive power because it doubles as defense and we have a quaint get-out-of-jail-for-a-small-fee card in Heavenly Guardian Defense. </span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">As long as we can hit with withering attacks or withering counters, we should be able to keep up a decent initiative pool to defend any such attack at our leisure. Part of this is starting with as hefty a pool as possible. Our reliance on DEX will factor well into combat movement rolls as well, making it hard to break away. One weakness is no charm support for snap movements, if a ranger attacker can pull away, we are in a seriously dangerous position... But there is a charm for that too. </span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b>Attributes: </b></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">We're going full-on twink here and dumping physical as primary, social as tertiary. </span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">I'm leaving Int and Per at 2 simply because I can't stand to have an Int 1 character... for some reason.</span></span><br /> <i><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Str 3, Dex 5, Sta 3; Cha 3, Man 1, App 3; Per 2, Int 2, Wit 5</span></span></i><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b>Abilities:</b> Numbers in brackets are points bought with bonus points. </span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Took all the important bits for combat and a smattering of one dot skills to support background (cause I felt like I had to). </span></span><br /> <i><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Melee 3 (+2) - Specialty: Swords; </span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Awareness 3 (+1) - Specialty: Strike First; </span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Socialize 3; </span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Brawl 3; </span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Dodge 3 - Specialty: Disengage; </span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Athletics 3 - Specialty: Rush; </span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Resistance 3; </span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Integrity 3; </span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Linguistics 1; </span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Lore 1; </span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Bureaucracy 1; </span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">War 1</span></span></i><br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Merits: </span></span></b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Medium weapon for superior defense, I went for heavy armour solely for the hardness (though the soak is nice too) and offset the mobility penalty with fleet of foot and my specialties. That's 11 motes committed though, ouch. This build initially had two daiklaives for the clash bonus but the motes lost were not worth it. </span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Splurged on two WP to fuel my best charms. </span></span><br /> <i><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Artifact 3 (Red Jade Daiklaive)</span></span></i><br /> <i><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Artifact 3 (Red Jade Reinforced Breastplate)</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Fleet of Foot 4</span></span></i><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><i>Willpower 5 (+2)</i></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Now the meat- </span></span><br /> <b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Charms: </span></span></b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">I bracketed ones I felt I could switch out. I'm uncertain if I should completely forgo the 'attack more people at once' charms because it might come in handy for later battles. Call the blade is purely for the daring disarm gambit and I feel a little too necessary to sub out, it's bracketed because it's such an edge case but disarming the Melee Supernal negates their entire kit so... Yeah... </span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">I considered grabbing Iron Raptor to deal with ranged attackers but I don't want to put myself in a situation where I've reset to base and haven't killed them while they are at medium range or more. I feel I would be crashed and killed soon after. </span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">I have forgone the defend-other branch as it is useless for this particular scenario. </span></span><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"><i><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Dipping Swallow Defense; Bulwark Stance; Excellent Strike; Fire and Stones Strike; </span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">One Weapon, Two Blows; (Peony Blossom Technique); Solar Counterattack; (Call the Blade); (Rising Sun Slash); Iron Whirlwind Attack; Five-Fold Bulwark Stance; Heavenly Guardian Defense; Hail-Shattering Practice; Invincible Fury of the Dawn; Perfect Strike Discipline; Flashing Edge of Dawn; Fervent Blow</span></span></i></div> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b>General Strategy:</b> I'll be looking to mostly just not get hit. Most of the kit is built around hard offense with a smattering of defensive charms. I have two avenues, if I hit first I can open up with many multiple attacks and if I don't hit first, the counterattack tree sets off the reflexive hurricane. I grabbed HGD to burn away those few attacks that might get through and threaten to deal some real damage. Combat movement pools are at a comfortable size as the penalties have already been accounted for. </span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">If I end up tweaking anything before Saturday's match, I'll let you know. Tomorrow I should have up the Brawler's Build.</span></span><br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>(10chars)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2721-elkovash","name":"Elkovash","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2721_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"528"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-05T13:53:26-07:00","id":883187,"title":"","content":"May I heavily suggest you switch to a goremaul from the daiklave? The amazing synergy of one weapon, two blows and a smashing (for prone) weapon can't be undervalued especially with a multiple hit strategy like yours.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1635-citadel97501","name":"Citadel97501","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"544"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-05T14:50:39-07:00","id":883226,"title":"","content":"Interesting weapon choice. I would have thought that medium mundane for parrying, artifact light for attacking would be a more powerful choice.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Some of me humble homebrew for ex3:<br /> <span style=\"font-size:10px\"><a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1hOOjEGyoq3owLoUwIwTfWKTffzo_udsiUTwomw7wudA/edit#\" target=\"_blank\">Artifacts for Crumple's DB homebrew</a><br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1tI2T1Re0G8QOuoXkH7Y4PrKQxk1BPEGpbi82SpkTyIw/edit\" target=\"_blank\">Some Lintha QCs</a><br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1O2I_2iWTCflJ36ggkDvjTeXmzFsGHKRxAi6L_Ry6g4w/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">A Wyld Behemoth</a></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8838-tds","name":"TDS","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"275"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-05T15:13:42-07:00","id":883242,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TDS</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/880699-peach-the-great-solar-exalted-tournament?p=883226#post883226\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Interesting weapon choice. I would have thought that medium mundane for parrying, artifact light for attacking would be a more powerful choice.</div> </div> </div> </div>Value judgement on my part. This build has to last me through the whole tournament and I'm expecting to come up against more soak heavy builds (given the ease of doing so) than defense heavy builds. I feel abase of 14 dice to wither is *enough* to threaten most people with a strike so I'll be relying more on the added damage form overwhelming than thresholds. <br /> <br /> I have been hard considering a Goremaul instead but I'm unsure if I want to take up another piece of kit that sucks away my initiative. That stuff is not just my damage, it's my lifeline. Something to ponder.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>(10chars)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2721-elkovash","name":"Elkovash","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2721_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"528"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-05T23:49:42-07:00","id":883521,"title":"","content":"I was going to offer to make a Survival character, but then I realized that there's basically nothing to do there. Get a Tyrant Lizard, buy Deadly Predator Method and all prereqs. Get a bow or something so that you can make a few attacks while your lizard does the real work. Only weakness is that DPM isn't nearly as impressive at E1 as it later will be.<br /> <br /> One question: if a character has a training Charm like Tiger-Warrior Training Technique, can they use it on their minions before the duel starts?<br /> <br /> Anyway, when the Ride character comes up I have a build in mind for them. Get a ranged weapon and a mount with +4 Speed. Use Supernal Lash Discipline to get +8 Speed. Use Immortal Charger's Gallop and Elusive Mount Technique to reflexively disengage from melee fighters with 8 bonus successes. Use Speed-Fury Focus to get those successes on Join Battle too, or at least to get as many successes as your dice cap allows. Use Thrown to attack so that you can take on archers in melee and melee fighters at range. Use other Ride Charms to generate initiative through your mount and to make it nearly unkillable.<br /> <br /> Ideally you'd want a steed with ranged attacks. Maybe a fire-breathing elemental-blooded simhata? Familiar 3 allows for stuff like that, after all.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/797631-why-craft-sucks-how-i-fixed-it\" target=\"_blank\">EX3 Craft Rewrite</a><br /> <br /> Sanctaphrax is not a person<br /> -Chejop Kejak","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1154-sanctaphrax","name":"Sanctaphrax","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1154_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1460"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-06T00:34:51-07:00","id":883548,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sanctaphrax</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/880699-peach-the-great-solar-exalted-tournament?p=883521#post883521\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I was going to offer to make a Survival character, but then I realized that there's basically nothing to do there. Get a Tyrant Lizard, buy Deadly Predator Method and all prereqs. Get a bow or something so that you can make a few attacks while your lizard does the real work. Only weakness is that DPM isn't nearly as impressive at E1 as it later will be.<br /> <br /> One question: if a character has a training Charm like Tiger-Warrior Training Technique, can they use it on their minions before the duel starts?<br /> <br /> Anyway, when the Ride character comes up I have a build in mind for them. Get a ranged weapon and a mount with +4 Speed. Use Supernal Lash Discipline to get +8 Speed. Use Immortal Charger's Gallop and Elusive Mount Technique to reflexively disengage from melee fighters with 8 bonus successes. Use Speed-Fury Focus to get those successes on Join Battle too, or at least to get as many successes as your dice cap allows. Use Thrown to attack so that you can take on archers in melee and melee fighters at range. Use other Ride Charms to generate initiative through your mount and to make it nearly unkillable.<br /> <br /> Ideally you'd want a steed with ranged attacks. Maybe a fire-breathing elemental-blooded simhata? Familiar 3 allows for stuff like that, after all.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'd prefer to try and stick with printed material, simply because I don't want my novice home brew to get in the way of this ridiculous experiment. =P<br /> <br /> As for charms, I guess we'll assume that so long as it doesn't have an EXP cost, you can have used it prior to the match to sure up your followers/familiar. <br /> <br /> If you'd like to submit a build ahead of time, please feel free!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>(10chars)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2721-elkovash","name":"Elkovash","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2721_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"528"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-06T12:31:20-07:00","id":883984,"title":"","content":"Hm. That's inconvenient for the Ride guy, especially since the Simhata isn't in the book anymore.<br /> <br /> Ah well. Using a horse isn't the end of the world. Probably less optimal than using a tyrant lizard but I don't want the Ride guy to be so similar to the Survival guy.<br /> <br /> Would you let someone wield a sky-cutter while mounted?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/797631-why-craft-sucks-how-i-fixed-it\" target=\"_blank\">EX3 Craft Rewrite</a><br /> <br /> Sanctaphrax is not a person<br /> -Chejop Kejak","edited":{"userid":1154,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1154-sanctaphrax","user":"Sanctaphrax","date":". 05-06-2016, 03:35 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1154-sanctaphrax","name":"Sanctaphrax","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1154_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1460"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-06T12:39:02-07:00","id":883993,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sanctaphrax</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/880699-peach-the-great-solar-exalted-tournament?p=883984#post883984\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hm. That's inconvenient for the Ride guy, especially since the Simhata isn't in the book anymore.<br /> <br /> Ah well. Using a horse isn't the end of the world. Probably less optimal than using a tyrant lizard but I don't want the Ride guy to be so similar to the Survival guy.<br /> <br /> Would you let someone wield a sky-cutter while mounted?</div> </div> </div> </div>I admit I haven't read the stats for the creatures as well as others, but I feel like an Ox-Dragon would be a rad Ride steed.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I post Artifacts in <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/823884-3e-the-artifact-and-evocation-workshop\" target=\"_blank\">this thread</a>. How I make them is in <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/828820-how-to-write-artifacts-and-evocations\" target=\"_blank\">this thread</a>.<br /> I have made many tools and other things for 3rd Edition. I now host all of my creations on my Google site: <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/unsungherovault/home\" target=\"_blank\">The Vault of the Unsung Hero</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/368-the-unsung-hero","name":"The Unsung Hero","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar368_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2288"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-06T18:21:47-07:00","id":884220,"title":"","content":"Unfortunately it's slower than a horse and not that good at fighting. 9 dice to hit won't cut it in a tournament full of people with defenses of 6-7. So even though it does lots of damage and has lots of health levels, I don't think it's a great choice.<br /> <br /> On all these characters, more dots of Cult would've been better than buying wp with BP. But it felt cheesy.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Eclipse Ride Guy</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Attributes: Strength 3, Dexterity 5, Stamina 3, Charisma 3, Manipulation 2, Appearance 2, Perception 3, Intelligence 1, Wits 5<br /> Abilities: Ride (Horses) 5, Thrown (Boomerang) 5, Awareness (Join battle) 5, Resistance 4, Integrity (Battle) 3, others<br /> Merits: Familiar 2 (Horse), Fast Reflexes 3, Artifact 3 (Sky-cutter), Cult 2<br /> Charms: Master Horseman's Technique (Harmony of Spirits Style, Spirit-Steadying Assurances, Blood Rider's Toughness), Flashing Thunderbolt Steed, Elusive Mount Technique, Wind-Racing Essence Infusion, Single Spirit Method, Seasoned Beast-Rider's Approach, Worthy Mount Technique, Mount Preservation Method, Immortal Charger's Gallop, Supernal Lash Discipline, Speed-Fury Focus, Immortal Rider's Advantage, Woe and Storm Evasion, Resilience of the Chosen Mount, Wrathful Mount Invigoration <br /> Willpower: 9<br /> Strategy: Open up with Supernal Lash Discipline, Seasoned Beast-Rider's Approach, and Speed-Fury Focus. Against a melee opponent, stay away. Against a ranged opponent, get in close.</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Zenith Survival Guy</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Attributes: Strength 3, Dexterity 5, Stamina 3, Charisma 5, Manipulation 1, Appearance 1, Perception 3, Intelligence 1, Wits 5<br /> Abilities: Survival (Dinosaurs) 5, Archery (Longbow) 5, Dodge (Distracting lizard) 5, Awareness 5, Resistance 4, Athletics 3, Integrity (Battle) 3, others<br /> Merits: Familiar 3 (Tyrant Lizard), Artifact 3 (Powerbow), Cult 4<br /> Charms: Friendship With Animals Approach, Spirit-Tied Pet, Beast-Mastering Behavior, Bestial Traits Technique, Deadly Onslaught Coordination, Hide-Hardening Practice, Life of the Aurochs, Familiar-Honing Instruction, Ambush Predator Style, Red-Toothed Execution Order, Saga Beast Virtue (Venomous 4, Poisoned Body 5. Unusual Hide 5), Force-Building Predator Style, Crimson Talon Vigor, Deadly Predator Method, one other Charm that doesn't matter<br /> Willpower: 8<br /> Strategy: Open by ordering the lizard into combat with Familar-Honing Instruction and Ambush Predator Style. Use Saga Beast Virtue and Deadly Predator Method. Send it in to fight while you sit back, fire arrows, and use Familiar-Honing Instruction. I considered adding more Familiars but it seemed a bit much.</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dawn War Guy</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Attributes: Strength 1, Dexterity 5, Stamina 5, Charisma 5, Manipulation 1, Appearance 1, Perception 3, Intelligence 1, Wits 5<br /> Abilities: War (Orders) 5, Melee (Shield) 5, Awareness 5, Resistance 4, Athletics 3, Integrity (Battle) 3, Dodge 3, others<br /> Merits: Command 5, Retainer 2, Artifact 3 (Heavy armour)<br /> Charms: All War Charms except Battle-Visionary's Foresight and Immortal Commander's Presence.<br /> Willpower: 9<br /> Strategy: Use Command to get 5 Size 5 battle groups and Retainer to get an officer to help you lead them. Use TWTT to make them all Elite. Sit back and give Order actions while your army fights, secure in the knowledge that even if most of your Charms are useless your massive army more than makes up for it.</div> </div> </div> </div>Here's the template I used, in case someone wants it:<br /> <br /> Attributes: Strength , Dexterity 5, Stamina , Charisma , Manipulation , Appearance , Perception , Intelligence , Wits <br /> Abilities: Awareness , Resistance , Athletics , Integrity<br /> Merits:<br /> Charms:<br /> Willpower:<br /> Strategy:","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/797631-why-craft-sucks-how-i-fixed-it\" target=\"_blank\">EX3 Craft Rewrite</a><br /> <br /> Sanctaphrax is not a person<br /> -Chejop Kejak","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1154-sanctaphrax","name":"Sanctaphrax","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1154_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1460"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-07T00:21:52-07:00","id":884434,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"font-size:20px\">Samiel - The Glorious Golden Fist of Nexus (Brawl Supernal, Dawn Caste, Solar Exalted)</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">From the depths of the Nexus fighting pits comes the Glorious Golden Fist, emperor of the ring and undisputed champion of the underbelly fight circuit. He found himself chosen by the Great god of Excellence when the seedier side of the criminal elements present in the pits tried to force him to throw a bout to make ridiculous profit, and turned murderous when he denied them their victory.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Build: </span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">This build was put together by my player, but instead of cheesing out on an ultimate build he templated from his current character and just changed up his charms.His focus is inflicting insurmountable penalties on his opponent from a barrage of fearsome attacks, eroding them into no challenge at all.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Brawl is heavy on the offensive side of Solar prowess and so lacks a steady defensive measure. There is the benefit of his long-game made to wear down his opponent before knocking them into next week, but he needs to ensure he can last past the first few bouts to bring that strength to bear. </span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Attributes:</span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"> Samiel is an experienced character so we had to wheel back some of his stats that he\u2019d increased since the chronicle began. The focus on stamina was to increase soak as high as possible (he used to be a heavy resistance-type solar with the Solar Hero Martial Arts style, back when we played 2.5)</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><i>Str 3, Dex 4, Sta 4; Cha 3, Man 1, App 3; Per 3, Int 2, Wit 4</i></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Abilities:</span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"> Numbers in brackets are points bought with bonus points. As above, this is his character\u2019s skill spread so it\u2019s not fully optimized, but he has all the important bits. </span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><i>Athletics 3 (+1) - Specialty: Feats of Strength; Awareness 3 (+2) - Specialty: Hidden Enemies; Brawl 3 (+2) - Specialty: Punching; Resistance 3 (+2) - Specialty: Tireless; Integrity 3; Investigation 2; Linguistics 1; Socialize 1; Medicine 2; Performance 3; Presence 3</i></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Merits: </span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Artifact armour to increase survivability, Pain Tolerance to reduce wound penalties if he does take damage. The rest is a bit of a no-show since it was carried over and not optimized. </span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><i>Artifact 3 (Articulated Plate)</i></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><i>Pain Tolerance 4</i></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><i>Language 1</i></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><i>Influence 2</i></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><i>Willpower 5 (+2)</i></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Now the meat- </span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Charms: </span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">I didn\u2019t ask my player much about why he chose what he chose, I thought he was going to go the grappling route but he chose to jump down the giant hammer fists route instead. This is a build to do damage and crush the opponent a little more with every turn.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><i>Ferocious Jab; Fists of Iron; Iron Body Focus; Ox-Stunning Blow; Thunderclap Rush; Falling Hammer Strike; Hammer on Iron Technique; Fivefold Fury Onslaught; Rampaging Berserk Attack; Heaven Fury Smite; Burning Fist Burial; Adamantine Fists of Battle x2; Incarnated Fury Attack; Force Rending Strike; Knock Out Blow; Cancel The Apocalypse</i></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">General Strategy:</span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"> I\u2019ve said this a few times already, but this build is made to penalize you for facing it. It has to hit hard or go home though, because without the penalties it deals in place, its survivability suffers immensely. He would benefit most from going first and determining the course of the battle from the outset.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Through the magic power of Random Chance, the duelists are being transported to the field of Battle chosen;<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:28px\">Wide-Open Plains</span></span></span><br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>(10chars)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2721-elkovash","name":"Elkovash","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2721_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"528"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-07T01:11:54-07:00","id":884457,"title":"","content":"My money's on Katsuko. Partly because she's got 2 more points of Parry. Also partly because Fivefold Bulwark Stance makes the whole Onslaught thing a lot less impressive, Heavenly Guardian Defense makes Incarnated Fury Attack a lot less impressive, and just having a high Parry makes Rampage-Berserker Attack and Burning Fist Burial a lot less impressive. Meanwhile, most of Katsuko's Charms look like they should work normally against Samiel. She can probably put a wound penalty on him right away with Flashing Edge Of Dawn.<br /> <br /> I think Samiel's best bet is probably to try and pile up his Ferocious Jab damage bonus and then maybe go for a big Ox-Stunning or Knockout Blow.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/797631-why-craft-sucks-how-i-fixed-it\" target=\"_blank\">EX3 Craft Rewrite</a><br /> <br /> Sanctaphrax is not a person<br /> -Chejop Kejak","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1154-sanctaphrax","name":"Sanctaphrax","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1154_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1460"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-07T02:20:10-07:00","id":884483,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"font-size:8px\">System Mechanics in Spoiler Tags</span><br /> <br /> The Arena of the Fifth Hand shimmers with its brilliant magics, shifting the space to that of a large rolling plain, nothing but grasses for miles around. Katsuko and Samiel both tense for the beginning of battle as the great horn blows, signaling the beginning of their bout.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">Katsuko and Samiel have chosen to begin at Close Range to each other and roll join battle. Katsuko rolls 3 and Samiel rolls 6.</div></div> </div> </div></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Samiel, digging his heels into the soft ground, lunges forwards and winds back his fist, almost bending his body in half before rocketing it forwards in a ferocious first strike; thrusting his fists into the space Katsuko occupied again and again.</span></span><br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Samiel Makes <b>Withering </b>attack and declares the following charms; <i>Ox Stunning Blow</i>, <i>Falling Hammer Strike</i> and a <i>Full Brawl Excellency</i>, adding <i>Adamantine fists of Battle</i> and <i>Fists of Iron</i> at the last moment.</span></span></div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Katsuko rolls the hilt of her blade about in her fingers, snapping her hand hard around it at the last moment, springing the blade up from its casual position and interposing it between them as she circles Samiel and makes the blade dance with her.</span></span><br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Katsuko declares Parry as her Defence. Activating the following charm, <i>Perfect Strike Discipline</i>, to add a full Melee excellency to her Parry Defence. Increasing it to 11.<br /> <br /> Samiel rolls 23 dice, 5 4 9 9 10 10 3 8 9 2 7 9 9 9 4 6 8 3 8 1 3 6 = with 15 successes for 4 threshold successes. Raw damage is 15 +1 for <i>Ox Stunning Blow</i> - Because of the effect of <i>Ox-Stunning Blow</i>, Katsuko can only soak this blow with her Stamina, but because of the effect of <i>Fists of Iron</i>, Samiel ignores up to 4 of Katsuko\u2019s soak, reducing it to 0 - due to his defining Principle of &quot;I spoil for a glorious and challenging battle&quot;.</span></span></div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Katsuko finds her moment, just as Samiel\u2019s barrage overtakes her and opens up her guard, her blade is brought flat against the underside of his shoulder joint, dragging the blade free as its edge runs through the small gap to be found there.</span></span><br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Katsuko declares - <i>Flashing Edge of Dawn</i> for 4m + 1wp, creating a new <b>withering </b>attack for Katsuko before damage is rolled.<br /> <br /> Samiel spends one willpower to increase his defence by 1 and 8m to increase it by a further 4; increasing his parry defence to 10</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Katsuko declares <i>Excellent Strike</i>, <i>Fire And Stones Strike</i>, and a <i>full Melee excellency</i> to increase her dice pool to 23 with one automatic success and rerolling all 1s.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">6 4 1 9 5 10 6 6 3 9 8 7 8 3 3 1 8 6 5 2 5 2 6 - 2 1s rerolled 10 8 = 12</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Katsuko declares <i>Rising Sun Slash</i>, for 1m, which adds 1 success and she gets to roll one more die 10 - increasing her roll to 15 successes granting her 5 thresholds and 20 raw damage.<br /> <br /> Samiel\u2019s Soak is 16, reducing her damage dice to 4. Katsuko\u2019s Overwhelming is 5, allowing her to roll 5 damage dice plus 3 for 8 total. 10 7 8 8 9 5 4 1 for 6 <b>withering </b>Damage - giving him 6 <b>decisive </b>damage dice and rolls 1 6 1 4 4 1 dealing no <b>decisive </b>damage.</span></span></div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">As her blade slides free, Katsuko\u2019s eyes narrow as her tongue clicks in frustration, she drew no blood despite the sureness of her strike. No matter, the motion tipped Samiel slightly off guard, his attacks slowing through their exchange of flashing Jade and glowing fist. Katsuko takes the opportunity between moments so spin on her heel, flinging the sharp edge of her blade repeatedly against the hauberk of his armour.</span></span><br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Katsuko\u2019s Initiative is now higher than Samiel\u2019s - so she declares <i>One Weapon, Two Blows</i>, another <b>Withering </b>Attack empowered by <i>Excellent Strike</i> for 3m leaving her with 11m.<br /> <br /> Samiel declares, <i>Full Brawl Excellency</i> for a total defence of 9 due to onslaught penalties.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Katsuko rolls 14 dice, 4 4 7 6 9 2 10 1 3 1 8 1 7 with 3 1s rerolled to 10 7 1, the 1 rerolled 5; for a total of 10 successes, Raw damage of 16 is reduced to 0 for an overwhelming damage roll of 5 dice, 10 10 8 3 3 for 5 <b>withering</b> damage.<br /> <br /> Samiel is Crashed, and Katsuko gains a +5 Break Bonus, plus 6i from her <b>withering</b> attack which pushes her up to 13i.</span></span></div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Katsuko\u2019s gambit has paid off, but now she must suffer the toll, catching his footing in the moment he flings forward his fists over and around her attacks to strike her hard against her core, a deliberate knuckle catching her in the side of the head, sending Katsuko reeling with the flash of white and spinning stars in her eyes.</span></span><br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div 